WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.221 --> 00:00:20.810
It was nearly Christmas by the time that all the financial arrangements were settled and I was able

2
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.171
to resign from the school.

3
00:00:23.391 --> 00:00:24.172
I had told St.

4
00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:27.834
John that I would remain as schoolmistress until he could find a replacement.

5
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:33.689
As I closed up the school for the holidays, I promised the girls that I would come every

6
00:00:33.749 --> 00:00:35.470
week and teach them for an hour.

7
00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:39.673
Watching my students file out of the school, St.

8
00:00:39.693 --> 00:00:42.014
John said to me, "What are you going to do now?"

9
00:00:42.034 --> 00:00:46.217
"I intend to be as active as I can," I replied.

10
00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:50.459
"First I must beg you to let Hannah come with me to Moor House.

11
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.702
Diana and Mary will be home in a week, and I want to have everything in order for

12
00:00:55.742 --> 00:00:56.403
their arrival."

13
00:00:57.643 --> 00:00:58.664
St. John looked puzzled.

14
00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:02.498
"I don't understand what employment you're proposing for yourself.

15
00:01:03.839 --> 00:01:05.320
What is your aim in life now?"

16
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:11.625
"My first aim will be to clean Moor House from top to bottom; my next will be to

17
00:01:11.705 --> 00:01:18.630
polish it until everything gleams; my third will be to arrange every piece of furniture with mathematical precision.

18
00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:23.054
Afterward Hannah and I will spend two days in the kitchen baking."

19
00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:25.876
I smiled with satisfaction.

20
00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:33.086
"In short, my aim is to have everything in perfect readiness for Diana and Mary's arrival next Thursday."

21
00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:37.407
St. John smiled but still managed to look dissatisfied.

22
00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:43.308
"That's all very well for the present, but I hope you'll soon look beyond household tasks and sisterly

23
00:01:43.348 --> 00:01:46.409
society." I did not understand him.

24
00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:51.451
"I'm prepared to be as content as a queen, and you're trying to make me restless.

25
00:01:51.631 --> 00:01:52.471
For what purpose?"

26
00:01:52.491 --> 00:01:56.412
"For the purpose of using the talents that God has given you."

27
00:01:58.316 --> 00:02:04.121
But working alongside Hannah, I was content, and when Thursday came at last, everything was ready.

28
00:02:05.423 --> 00:02:06.664
St. John arrived first.

29
00:02:06.684 --> 00:02:09.786
"Are you finished with housemaid's work?"

30
00:02:10.207 --> 00:02:11.908
he asked when he found me in the kitchen.

31
00:02:11.928 --> 00:02:16.092
"Come see the results of my labors," I said cheerfully.

32
00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:20.076
With great difficulty I persuaded him to tour the house.

33
00:02:21.372 --> 00:02:26.114
As we wandered upstairs and down, he said that I must have gone to a great deal of

34
00:02:26.194 --> 00:02:29.376
trouble to have made so much progress in so little time.

35
00:02:30.596 --> 00:02:33.497
But he didn't express any pleasure in my improvements.

36
00:02:34.778 --> 00:02:36.259
His silence disturbed me.

37
00:02:36.979 --> 00:02:42.041
I had replaced some curtains and furniture, and I thought perhaps he was upset by these changes.

38
00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.802
"Not at all," he said.

39
00:02:44.822 --> 00:02:48.004
"You've been quite respectful of the old house.

40
00:02:50.108 --> 00:02:53.150
I only fear that you've bestowed more thought on it than it deserves."

41
00:02:54.471 --> 00:02:56.572
Then he asked me where a certain book was.

42
00:02:57.853 --> 00:03:01.355
I removed it from a shelf, and he withdrew to a window seat to read.

43
00:03:02.576 --> 00:03:09.000
Watching him, I contemplated his lack of pleasure in my improvements to his family home and suddenly realized

44
00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.241
how trying it would be to be his wife.

45
00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:17.364
Diana and Mary soon arrived, bringing joy to Moor House.

46
00:03:17.384 --> 00:03:23.306
Unlike their brother, they were delighted with the new drapery and fresh carpets, and they generously expressed their

47
00:03:23.346 --> 00:03:27.468
gratitude. I'm afraid that the ensuing week tried St.

48
00:03:27.568 --> 00:03:28.468
John's patience.

49
00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:34.830
It was Christmas week, and we did nothing but spend it in a sort of merry domestic dissipation.

50
00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.652
St. John did not rebuke us for our high spirits, but he was seldom home.

51
00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:47.371
He had the unsociable habit of reading at meals, and one morning at breakfast, Diana asked him about

52
00:03:47.431 --> 00:03:48.071
his plans.

53
00:03:48.091 --> 00:03:52.733
"I'm planning to leave for India in the coming year," he responded.

54
00:03:52.753 --> 00:03:55.074
"And Rosamond Oliver?"

55
00:03:55.494 --> 00:03:56.175
asked Mary.

56
00:03:57.515 --> 00:04:02.137
St. John closed his book and said calmly, "Rosamond Oliver is about to be married."

57
00:04:03.398 --> 00:04:08.120
His sisters and I looked at each other and then at him, but his face remained unchanged.

58
00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:15.334
The next time we were alone, I was tempted to ask if Miss Oliver's marriage distressed him, but

59
00:04:15.374 --> 00:04:17.134
he seemed to need little sympathy.

60
00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:22.936
As his sisters and I resumed our usual quiet activities, he spent more time with us.

61
00:04:24.236 --> 00:04:28.857
He had promised to treat me as a sister, but he confided in me less often than when

62
00:04:28.937 --> 00:04:31.058
I had been merely the village schoolmistress.

63
00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:37.160
One afternoon I was not able to make my usual visit to the village school because I had

64
00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:37.580
a cold.

65
00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.502
Mary and Diana went in my place.

66
00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:45.185
I sat reading German poetry while St.

67
00:04:45.205 --> 00:04:49.028
John studied Hindustani, the language he would need as a missionary.

68
00:04:50.268 --> 00:04:53.011
When I looked up for a moment, I saw him staring at me.

69
00:04:53.031 --> 00:04:57.574
"Jane, I want you to give up German and learn Hindustani."

70
00:04:59.095 --> 00:05:04.800
"Why?" He explained that it would greatly help him to have a pupil with whom he could converse.

71
00:05:05.952 --> 00:05:11.214
For quite some time he had been considering asking me or his sisters, but he had settled on

72
00:05:11.274 --> 00:05:14.296
me because I could sit at a task the longest of the three.

73
00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:18.978
He was not a man to be lightly refused, so I consented.

74
00:05:20.218 --> 00:05:25.241
When Diana and Mary returned, they said that he never would have been able to persuade them to

75
00:05:25.281 --> 00:05:27.442
take such a step, and he agreed.

76
00:05:28.742 --> 00:05:32.184
As the weeks passed, I began to feel that he was taking over my mind.

77
00:05:34.204 --> 00:05:38.445
I no longer felt that I could talk or laugh freely in front of him because that annoyed

78
00:05:38.505 --> 00:05:44.387
him. I wanted to please him more every day, but I also felt that I had to disown

79
00:05:44.507 --> 00:05:45.988
half of myself to do so.

80
00:05:47.308 --> 00:05:50.169
Perhaps, reader, you think that I had forgotten Mr.

81
00:05:50.269 --> 00:05:53.270
Rochester amid these changes of place and fortune.

82
00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.591
Not for a moment.

83
00:05:56.811 --> 00:06:00.212
The craving to know what had become of him followed me everywhere.

84
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:07.160
When I was the village schoolmistress, I had reentered my cottage every evening wondering about his fate, and

85
00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.042
now at Moor House, I brooded over it each night in my bedroom.

86
00:06:12.263 --> 00:06:14.244
In the course of my correspondence with Mr.

87
00:06:14.284 --> 00:06:18.547
Briggs about my uncle's will, I had inquired if he knew anything about Mr.

88
00:06:18.587 --> 00:06:21.028
Rochester's present residence and state of health.

89
00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:23.770
But as St.

90
00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.591
John had conjectured, Mr.

91
00:06:25.611 --> 00:06:26.492
Briggs knew nothing.

92
00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:28.641
I then wrote to Mrs.

93
00:06:28.681 --> 00:06:31.423
Fairfax, entreating her for information about Mr.

94
00:06:31.463 --> 00:06:36.366
Rochester. I felt sure that my letter would elicit a prompt response.

95
00:06:37.647 --> 00:06:40.669
I was astonished when two weeks passed without a reply.

96
00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:47.974
When two months wore away, and day after day the post arrived and brought me nothing, I fell

97
00:06:48.054 --> 00:06:49.755
prey to the keenest anxiety.

98
00:06:51.016 --> 00:06:54.418
I wrote again because there was a chance that my first letter had gone astray.

99
00:06:55.659 --> 00:07:00.127
For a few weeks I was hopeful, but my hope faded when not a word reached me.

100
00:07:01.429 --> 00:07:08.717
After six months wasted in vain expectancy, my hope died out completely, and I felt dark indeed.
